# Test: ze doctor --json reports on the VPP linux_cp plugin when vpp.lcp is on.
# VALIDATES: fixit-vpp-lcp-reachability AC-6 and AC-7 -- the check is reachable
# from the USER entry point (registration, phase, platform filtering and the
# diagnostic code all have to line up), and a FAILED probe degrades to a
# warning that names the probe rather than claiming the plugin is missing.
# PREVENTS: the check regressing to error-on-probe-failure. `vppctl` exits
# non-zero for an absent binary, an absent socket and a wedged VPP alike, and
# none of those is evidence about which plugins VPP loaded -- reporting an
# error there would tell an operator to rebuild VPP when the real problem is
# that VPP is not running. This host has no vppctl, so it exercises exactly
# that path.
# Required by ai/rules/doctor-checks.md ("Test Requirement": unit AND
# functional), modelled on test/ui/doctor-ipsec-iface.ci.
#
# needs-linux: the check returns early on any non-Linux host (VPP is
# Linux-only, and AC-11 requires that no probe is opened there), so on darwin
# this would assert an absence that is true for the wrong reason.
option=needs-linux

tmpfs=vpp-lcp.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
    backend vpp
}

vpp {
    lcp {
        enabled true
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json vpp-lcp.conf
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-vpp-lcp-plugin
expect=stdout:contains=could not be probed
